                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to an archdeacon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28e3b6e7-10db-499b-ae83-79accdf2d339",
                                "sense_id": "f2727913-44a2-3cca-8591-51a62544a915",
                                "text": "[…] they giue good allowance of Episcopal dignitie & their iurisdiction but they vtterly disallow and would gladly infringe Archidiaconall power and weaken that first."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f67a428-99c5-4d05-96b4-cfda0a99566c",
                                "sense_id": "f2727913-44a2-3cca-8591-51a62544a915",
                                "text": "1787, William Hutchinson, The History and Antiquities of the County Palatine, of Durham, Newcastle: S. Hodgson, Volume 2, pp. 88-89,\n[…] by compromise it was settled, that the prior should enjoy archidiaconal jurisdiction in the churches of Jarrow and Weremouth, and Goldesburgh throughout the rest for life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73083b2f-39d1-446a-8764-961d792e100b",
                                "sense_id": "f2727913-44a2-3cca-8591-51a62544a915",
                                "text": "[…] his Phi Beta Kappa key shone against a spotty black vest; he smelled of old pipes; he was altogether funereal and archidiaconal; and to real-estate brokerage and the jobbing of bathroom-fixtures he added an aroma of sanctity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00d9d2f8-55ce-48cd-bdf2-6023fd2ab0bd",
                                "sense_id": "f2727913-44a2-3cca-8591-51a62544a915",
                                "text": "With Father Jolliffe cringing under the archidiaconal disapproval it ought to have been a chilling moment and, by Treacher at least, savoured and briefly enjoyed […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8062424-14c5-4ad6-8dd9-6a6f95c0eb11",
                                "sense_id": "f2727913-44a2-3cca-8591-51a62544a915",
                                "text": "Hicks wrote in the diary in July 1913 about the arrangements for the two forthcoming archidiaconal installations."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
